# Model of the figure 'moving-average'. Edit this file; `kokeb-docs figures` draws it. Never edit the SVGs.
kind: pipeline
id: moving-average
title: How Push and Average keep a running sum
alt: >-
  Flow of one Push call: the window-full check picks between counting up and subtracting the oldest sample, the
  sample is stored and added to the sum, and Average divides the sum by the count.
reads: >-
  Four columns from left to right: Check, Update, Store and Output. Push sample starts in the Check column as the
  question Window full. When the window is not full the Update step adds one to the count, and when it is full the
  Update step subtracts the oldest sample from the sum. Both paths reach the Store step, which stores the sample and
  adds it to the sum. The Output step, Average, divides the sum by the count.
print: landscape
sources:
  - docs/model/moving-average.pipeline.yml
columns:
  - id: check
    title: Check
    tone: amber
    items:
      - {id: full, title: "Push: window full?"}
  - id: update
    title: Update
    tone: violet
    items:
      - {id: count, title: count + 1}
      - {id: oldest, title: sum - oldest}
  - id: store
    title: Store
    tone: green
    items:
      - {id: store, title: "store, sum + sample"}
  - id: output
    title: Output
    tone: brand
    items:
      - {id: avg, title: "Average = sum / count"}
links:
  - {from: full, to: count, label: "no"}
  - {from: full, to: oldest, label: "yes"}
  - {from: count, to: store}
  - {from: oldest, to: store}
  - {from: store, to: avg}
